{"id": "EUVD-2026-86732", "enisaUuid": "6f45357a-3f75-38c0-87eb-341e73119db3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nieee802154: 6lowpan: fix NULL dereference in lowpan_newlink\n\nTUNSETLINK allows a TUN device to change its link-layer type to\nARPHRD_IEEE802154 without initializing ieee802154_ptr. lowpan_newlink()\nchecks only the device type before dereferencing the pointer, so an\nRTM_NEWLINK request can trigger a NULL pointer dereference.\n\nReject devices without ieee802154_ptr along with devices of the wrong type.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1760f21c32adce41af5ed5687200865d8feaaeb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5063b9354e6e285dae61e530b30458498444a914", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16d8e0b560d50cd1a9e6d77a9a154a94c4d6021e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/543994fa03c36a91d967a12c5c99cae74899504c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c7710af7ad9532b534f1c134c11b04dbe4e0e0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98ce5a42cde780ee0e40378607d4428c8fc12ec1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8528da2333ce05cf627f93425f9d05efb08b3146", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf79662bc85e820ac3b846e2f347da29fbf6ac95"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97601", "GHSA-mh2g-wr94-hfmw"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09e57439-fd73-30a1-890a-d9b40f12b248", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "17a72d40-df3f-381b-adfa-980bb62cb48b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "51e0e5d8124ece158927a4c2288c0929d3b53aa3 <bf79662bc85e820ac3b846e2f347da29fbf6ac95"}, {"id": "181b9d85-fc04-39ec-a760-68cd039e19c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "1f1b9d8d-eb14-3e24-ab0d-1f8b609ae052", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux